WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Sometimes your family, friends, or community can help.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.679
They can help you solve problems,

00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:06.640
which can lower some of the triggers.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.439
Your family might also try to talk more

00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:10.080
about good things that happened.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.439
This helps you enjoy those happy times more.

00:00:12.439 --> 00:00:14.880
Finally, you might start planning a fun event,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.519
and we'll try this later too.

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:18.879
Just like events affect kids in different ways,

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:22.240
these ways to help also work differently for each kid.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.039
For some kids, exercise helps,

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:25.560
but writing in a journal does not.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.199
For some, talking to friends helps,

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:29.400
but for others, it has to be a family member.

00:00:29.399 --> 00:00:32.839
And some kids can get help from a mental health professional.

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:35.719
This can be a school counselor or someone else in their community.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:37.039
These helpers have many names

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:39.679
at counselors, social workers, or psychologists.

00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:41.640
Today, we will just call them counselors.

